Rationalize the numerator:
\[
\frac{\sqrt{x+1}-1}{x}
=
\frac{(\sqrt{x+1}-1)(\sqrt{x+1}+1)}
{x(\sqrt{x+1}+1)}
=
\frac{x}{x(\sqrt{x+1}+1)}
=
\frac{1}{\sqrt{x+1}+1}.
\]
Therefore,
\[
\lim_{x\to 0}\frac{\sqrt{x+1}-1}{x}
=
\frac{1}{\sqrt{1}+1}
=
\frac{1}{2}.
\]
For continuity at \(x=0\), we need \(k=\frac{1}{2}\).
